I don't know what is causing this, but there is a bug in the routines to
add up your gold talons after each turn.  Actually the bug also exists in
the budget routine.  The budget routine will print out the I have a net
income of whatever, and yet somehow it says that my total expected gold
will be smaller than the gold I have this turn, even if my net income is
positive!  This same problem occurs in the update.  Also, the charity
function doesn't seem to work and may be the problem.  Changes of 1% in
my charity change my expected income by about 9% of my net income!  This is
kind of a drag to say the least, because I have been unable to amass much
gold.  And no, this is not the result of having too few jewels.


